# MF Flow scraper environment overrides — copy to `.env` and edit.
# On the droplet this file MUST exist (the runner loads it at import via
# python-dotenv, so it works under cron's empty environment). chmod 600 .env
# because it may hold proxy credentials.
#
# Linux/droplet values are shown below. On Windows the two paths default to
# the developer's machine and can be left unset.

# ---- REQUIRED on the droplet ----------------------------------------------

# Source of truth for the MF list + scheme roster (the client's xlsx).
# Default (Windows dev box): C:\Users\aayus\OneDrive\Desktop\MF Flow (08062026).xlsx
INPUT_XLSX=/opt/mf-flow/input.xlsx

# Where downloaded portfolios land (<OUTPUT_ROOT>/<MF Name>/<Month YYYY>/...).
# Default: <project>/output
OUTPUT_ROOT=/opt/mf-flow/output

# ---- OPTIONAL: proxy for AMCs that block DigitalOcean IPs ------------------
# A few AMCs (DSP, HDFC file CDN) return Cloudflare 403 from DO data-center IPs.
# Route ONLY those hosts through a residential proxy; everything else stays
# direct. Leave both unset if you are not on a blocked ASN.
#
# MF_FLOW_PROXY=http://user:pass@residential-proxy.example.com:7777
# MF_FLOW_PROXY_HOSTS=dspim.com,hdfcfund.com,files.hdfcfund.com
#
# If MF_FLOW_PROXY is set WITHOUT MF_FLOW_PROXY_HOSTS, ALL traffic is proxied
# (debugging only — slower and unnecessary for most AMCs).
